  "name": "07_microphone_audio",
  "title": "Microphone audio upload",
  "description": "The PC uploads 0.5 s chunks of 16 kHz mono audio while the microphone is on. A retried chunk is ignored, a dropped chunk leaves a gap in the chunk numbers, and the event the server found in the audio carries the chunks' microphone generation and AEC status. After the microphone is turned off and on again, chunk numbers restart at 0 in the new generation. Audio bytes are not stored here: only each binary frame's JSON header is listed.",
